            },
            "body": [
              {
                "_type": "Expr",
                "_fields": {
                  "value": {
                    "_type": "Constant",
                    "_fields": {
                      "value": "\n    Normalize raw retrieval results into a canonical RetrievalResult.\n\n    Steps:\n        0. Apply meta_profile biases to RetrievalConfig.\n        1. Normalize raw dicts into {query, evidence, rank}.\n        2. Deduplicate identical (query, evidence) pairs.\n        3. Apply ranking strategy (bm25/dense/hybrid).\n        4. Rerank & fuse results (single-source).\n        5. Limit items to config.max_items.\n        6. Optionally filter for basic safety when heightened_caution.\n        7. Normalize to RAG-style items with metadata.\n        8. Return RetrievalResult with RetrievalItem objects.\n\n    This function does NOT call any external services; it operates on\n    already-fetched raw results (e.g., from a DB, vector store, or LLM).\n    ",
                      "kind": "None"
                    },
                    "_lineno": 248,
                    "_col_offset": 4
                  }
                },
                "_lineno": 248,
                "_col_offset": 4
              },
